-### VideoToolbox is off by default on Apple Silicon
-
-The VideoToolbox RGB decoder crashes on M1 and later, so `ENABLE_VIDEOTOOLBOX`
-defaults to `OFF` there and RGB decoding uses TurboJPEG. On Intel Macs it
-defaults to `ON`. See `ENABLE_VIDEOTOOLBOX` in `CMakeLists.txt`.
+### VideoToolbox JPEG decoding
+
+`ENABLE_VIDEOTOOLBOX` defaults to `ON` on every Mac. On Apple Silicon the colour
+JPEGs are then decoded by the media engine: about 1 ms of CPU per 1080p frame
+instead of 3-12 ms with TurboJPEG (M3 Ultra). Packets the decoder rejects are
+dropped, and if it keeps failing TurboJPEG takes over at run time
+(`PacketPipelineConfig::allow_fallback`). Earlier versions crashed on M1 and
+later because a rejected packet produced a frame with NULL data; that is fixed.
+Set `-DENABLE_VIDEOTOOLBOX=OFF`, or `LIBFREENECT2_RGB_PROCESSOR=turbojpeg` at run
+time, to use TurboJPEG.
 
 ### Architecture mismatch
 
