+/** @file vt_rgb_packet_processor.cpp VideoToolbox (hardware) JPEG decoder for macOS.
+ *
+ * On Apple Silicon the JPEG is decoded by the media engine: ~1 ms of CPU per
+ * 1080p frame instead of 3-12 ms with TurboJPEG. Decoded frames are IOSurface
+ * backed BGRA pixel buffers handed to the listener without a copy.
+ *
+ * The decoder used to crash on M1 and later: a packet the hardware decoder
+ * rejects (truncated or corrupt JPEG after a USB hiccup) produces no pixel
+ * buffer, and the old code still emitted a frame whose data was NULL. Now a
+ * rejected packet is dropped (like TurboJPEG does), a session the system
+ * invalidated (sleep, GPU reset) is recreated, and the processor reports
+ * itself unhealthy only after a run of failures, so RgbDecoderFallback can
+ * switch to TurboJPEG.
+ */
 
